WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:04.036
-The President and his allies
are now trying out

00:00:04.036 --> 00:00:06.206
the Ukraine whistle-blower
as one of Trump's

00:00:06.206 --> 00:00:08.708
own appointees admits there was
a quid pro quo.

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:11.177
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:13.313
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:18.117
You might remember that the
whole Ukraine scandal began

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:20.119
when an anonymous whistle-blower
in the Trump administration

00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:22.622
filed a complaint,
alleging that the President

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:25.291
had abused his power
to engage in a criminal act.

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:27.126
-From the whistle-blower
who says, "In the course

00:00:27.126 --> 00:00:29.562
of my official duties,
I have received information

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:31.631
from multiple U.S.
government officials

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:33.065
that the President
of the United States

00:00:33.065 --> 00:00:36.168
is using the power of his office
to solicit interference

00:00:36.168 --> 00:00:39.606
from a foreign country in the
2020 U.S. election."

00:00:39.606 --> 00:00:42.074
-This interference includes,
among other things,

00:00:42.074 --> 00:00:44.777
pressuring a foreign country
to investigate one

00:00:44.777 --> 00:00:47.847
of the president's main domestic
political rivals.

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:50.316
-According to a memo
by the whistle-blower,

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:52.218
a White House official
who listened in

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:55.021
on the call to Ukraine's
president described the call

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:59.058
as crazy, frightening, and
completely lacking in substance

00:00:59.058 --> 00:01:00.659
related to national security.

00:01:00.659 --> 00:01:04.464
-The official was visibly shaken
by what had transpired,

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:06.432
and in the official's view,
the President

00:01:06.432 --> 00:01:08.701
had clearly committed
a criminal act.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:11.070
-It is not hard for me
to believe that someone

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:12.372
in the Trump administration
witnessed

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:13.940
the President
commit a criminal act.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:15.842
Trump probably commits crimes
the way people

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:18.878
with Fitbits get in their steps.

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:22.115
"Oh no, I haven't gotten
my crimes in today.

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:23.816
I better go knock over
a liquor store.

00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:25.084
I'm so sorry about this.

00:01:25.084 --> 00:01:28.887
I'm -- I'm just doing it
to hit my goal."

00:01:28.887 --> 00:01:30.990
I mean, if there was
a whistle-blower complaint

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.593
for every crime Trump committed,
he'd have to hold another one

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:35.594
of those dumb press conferences
where he's surrounded

00:01:35.594 --> 00:01:37.030
by a giant stack of paper.

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:38.130
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:39.699
"And as you can see
from the sign,

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:43.269
these are just the crimes
I've committed today."

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:45.671
So, the whistle-blower is the
one who tipped everyone off

00:01:45.671 --> 00:01:47.640
to the fact that something
very corrupt had happened,

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.708
but since then, we've seen
the notes from the call.

00:01:49.708 --> 00:01:51.310
We've seen text messages
from officials

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:52.411
involved in the scheme.

00:01:52.411 --> 00:01:54.313
We've had Trump
and his Chief of Staff

00:01:54.313 --> 00:01:57.483
confess on TV, and we've had
one witness after another

00:01:57.483 --> 00:01:59.752
come forward, and provide
damning testimony.

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:01.387
We already have
all the evidence.

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:03.223
This is like if during
the O.J. trial they not only

00:02:03.223 --> 00:02:05.224
had the gloves,
but dozens of witnesses,

00:02:05.224 --> 00:02:08.227
a tape of O.J. confessing
and a note inside the gloves
that said,

00:02:08.227 --> 00:02:10.763
"If found at crime scene,
return to O.J. Simpson,

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:12.064
the murderer."

00:02:12.064 --> 00:02:13.299
[ Laughter and Applause ]

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:16.903
And yet -- and yet --
Trump and his allies

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:18.337
remain obsessed
with the whistle-blower.

00:02:18.337 --> 00:02:20.206
They've tried to paint
the whistle-blower as some sort

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:23.342
of shadowy, anti-Trump operative
who's biased against him.

00:02:23.342 --> 00:02:25.945
And Trump has repeatedly called
for the whistle-blower's

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:27.413
identity to be revealed.

00:02:27.413 --> 00:02:31.650
-I think that the whistle-blower
gave a lot of false information,

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:34.787
and you have to see who
the whistle-blower is.

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:38.557
Once I release the transcript,
which was almost immediately,

00:02:38.557 --> 00:02:40.960
the whistle-blower's report
was very wrong.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:44.797
So once I released that call,
I released a very detailed

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:47.033
version of that call,
all of a sudden

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:49.502
the whistle-blower's
report was incorrect,

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:51.871
and the whistle-blower
seems to have disappeared.

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:54.106
-No, the whistle-blower
did not disappear.

00:02:54.106 --> 00:02:56.909
The only people who can
disappear are David Copperfield

00:02:56.909 --> 00:02:59.312
and Steven Miller
if you expose him to garlic.

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:00.646
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.646 --> 00:03:02.815
Be gone, demon!

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:06.152
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:09.555 --> 00:03:13.459
Also, just because
you don't know someone

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:14.793
doesn't mean that person
has disappeared.

00:03:14.793 --> 00:03:18.331
The whistle-blower still exists.
They're just anonymous.

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:21.066
Trumps' like a dog who thinks
the tennis ball disappeared

00:03:21.066 --> 00:03:24.303
just because you rolled it
behind the couch.

00:03:24.303 --> 00:03:26.806
"What the hell? We were just
playing with that ball.

00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:28.407
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.407 --> 00:03:32.045
And now, thin air, poof,
gone forever."

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:34.981
We all have the actual
evidence now.

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:36.582
And yet, Trump and his allies

00:03:36.582 --> 00:03:38.017
are still obsessed
with the whistle-blower.

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:39.886
On Monday, Trump tweeted
the whistle-blower gave

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:42.322
false information, he must be
brought forward to testify.

00:03:42.322 --> 00:03:43.456
Written answers, not acceptable.

00:03:43.456 --> 00:03:44.923
So there you go.

00:03:44.923 --> 00:03:47.226
Trump wants the Ukraine
whistle-blower outed,

00:03:47.226 --> 00:03:50.229
and he says written questions
are not acceptable.

00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:52.431
Of course, when Trump had to
answer his own questions

00:03:52.431 --> 00:03:54.200
as part of Robert Mueller's
Russia investigation,

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:56.736
he felt a little different
about the acceptability

00:03:56.736 --> 00:03:58.738
of written answers,
even claiming that he

00:03:58.738 --> 00:04:00.172
personally wrote
the answers himself.

00:04:00.172 --> 00:04:01.241
-He hired 18 people.

00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:02.474
-Didn't answer questions
on obstruction.

00:04:02.474 --> 00:04:03.743
-Well, wait a minute.
I did answer questions.

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:06.278
I answered them in writing.
-Not on obstruction.

00:04:06.278 --> 00:04:08.413
-I don't know.
I answered a lot of questions.

00:04:08.413 --> 00:04:12.852
They gave me questions.
I answered them in writing.

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:16.155
About what?

00:04:16.155 --> 00:04:18.190
Yeah, my lawyers
aren't working on that.

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:19.859
I'm working on that.
I write the answers.

00:04:19.859 --> 00:04:22.161
My lawyers don't write answers.
I write answers.

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:24.163
-No, you don't. No.

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:25.865
No one believes you wrote
the answers.

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:27.900
for one thing, if Trump had
actually written the answers,

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.068
they'd be full of misspellings.

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:30.903
Trump has misspelled
his wife's name,

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:33.740
his own name,
the word "country,"

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:36.242
and the word "Republicans."

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:37.777
Can you imagine Robert Mueller

00:04:37.777 --> 00:04:39.077
trying to sift through
those answers?

00:04:39.077 --> 00:04:40.445
What are Ru-Publicans?

00:04:40.445 --> 00:04:42.748
Are those fans of RuPaul?

00:04:42.748 --> 00:04:45.117
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:45.117 --> 00:04:48.687
You see,
Republicans stand by Trump.

00:04:48.687 --> 00:04:52.391
Whereas, Ru-Publicans think it's
time for him to sashay away.

00:04:52.391 --> 00:04:53.926
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:53.926 --> 00:04:57.229
This obsession -- this obsession
with the whistle-blower's

00:04:57.229 --> 00:04:59.932
identity has now gone so far off
the rails that both Trump

00:04:59.932 --> 00:05:02.635
and his allies in Congress
like Kentucky Senator Rand Paul

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:04.570
are openly calling
on the media to find out

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:07.206
who the whistle-blower is,
and print their name.

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:08.307
-You know who it is.

00:05:08.307 --> 00:05:10.042
You just don't want
to report it.

00:05:10.042 --> 00:05:13.312
CNN knows who it is,
but you don't want to report it.

00:05:13.312 --> 00:05:16.648
And you know you'd be doing the
public a service if you did.

00:05:16.648 --> 00:05:19.618
-The whistle-blower needs
to come before Congress

00:05:19.618 --> 00:05:21.420
as a material witness.

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:27.627
I say tonight, to the media,
do your job and print his name.

00:05:27.627 --> 00:05:32.064
And I say to my colleagues,
if shifty Schiff will not let

00:05:32.064 --> 00:05:34.533
Hunter Biden come,
and if you will not bring

00:05:34.533 --> 00:05:37.570
the whistle-blower forward,
every Republican in Congress

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:40.939
should take a walk
and say this is a farce.

00:05:40.939 --> 00:05:42.275
-I agree with one part of that.

00:05:42.275 --> 00:05:44.076
Republicans should definitely
take a walk.

00:05:44.076 --> 00:05:47.079
Because it's always fun
to watch Republicans walk,

00:05:47.079 --> 00:05:50.449
just like when Trump wanders
around in circles

00:05:50.449 --> 00:05:54.453
on the White House lawn like a
retiree looking for crab grass.

00:05:54.453 --> 00:05:55.854
I mean, look at him.

00:05:55.854 --> 00:05:58.724
He should be carrying a rake
and a bottle of weed killer.

00:05:58.724 --> 00:06:00.993
Also, I love that when he gets
lost and doesn't know

00:06:00.993 --> 00:06:03.496
where to go, he just stands
completely still,

00:06:03.496 --> 00:06:06.965
hoping people forget
he's there.

00:06:06.965 --> 00:06:09.334
He's like an extra
on a movie set who forgot

00:06:09.334 --> 00:06:11.470
what he's supposed to do.

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:13.272
I'm pretty sure I saw him
once in the background

00:06:13.272 --> 00:06:15.941
of "Goodfellas."

00:06:15.941 --> 00:06:18.010
Look at him just standing there
trying to blend in

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:19.879
with the background
like a regular lizard

00:06:19.879 --> 00:06:21.247
who thinks he's a chameleon.

00:06:21.247 --> 00:06:22.347
[ Laughter ]

00:06:22.347 --> 00:06:25.585
"So lucky I turned Green."

00:06:25.585 --> 00:06:27.720
Trump and his allies are fixated
on the whistle-blower because

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:29.989
the actual evidence is damning
and they have no response.

00:06:29.989 --> 00:06:31.623
That's why their defense
keeps changing.

00:06:31.623 --> 00:06:34.860
For example, Trump and his GOP
allies went from insisting

00:06:34.860 --> 00:06:37.329
that he did nothing wrong
to arguing that there was

00:06:37.329 --> 00:06:39.198
no quid pro quo with Ukraine.

00:06:39.198 --> 00:06:41.233
Although,
Trump wasn't always clear

00:06:41.233 --> 00:06:43.502
on the exact wording
of the phrase.

00:06:43.502 --> 00:06:45.237
-There's no quid pro quo.

00:06:45.237 --> 00:06:47.573
No demand. No pressure.
No threat.

00:06:47.573 --> 00:06:50.476
-There's no quid pro quo.
There was no quid pro quo.

00:06:50.476 --> 00:06:51.810
-There is no quid pro quo.

00:06:51.877 --> 00:06:53.479
-There is no quid pro quo.

00:06:53.479 --> 00:06:55.314
-There was no quid pro quo.

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:58.016
-There was no quid pro quo.

00:06:58.016 --> 00:07:00.219
There was no quid pro quo.

00:07:00.219 --> 00:07:04.924
But listen to this,
there is no pro quo.

00:07:04.924 --> 00:07:07.192
[ Laughter ]
-That's right.

00:07:07.192 --> 00:07:09.095
There was no pro quo.

00:07:09.095 --> 00:07:13.766
So, doesn't that mean
there was a quid?

00:07:13.766 --> 00:07:16.502
No pro quo sounds like something
you'd say on a trip to Europe

00:07:16.502 --> 00:07:18.470
to explain you don't speak
the language.

00:07:18.470 --> 00:07:21.673
"Scusi, no pro quo.

00:07:21.673 --> 00:07:24.676
No pro quo, senor."

00:07:24.676 --> 00:07:26.512
But that's been the Republican
argument this whole time.

00:07:26.512 --> 00:07:28.381
There was no quid pro quo.

00:07:28.381 --> 00:07:30.016
Then yesterday, we found out
that one of Trump's

00:07:30.016 --> 00:07:32.651
own appointees said
there was a quid pro quo.

00:07:32.651 --> 00:07:35.120
And yet, instead of listening
to that evidence,

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:36.956
Republican Senator
Lindsey Graham dismissed

00:07:36.956 --> 00:07:38.891
the entire impeachment inquiry
all together.

00:07:38.891 --> 00:07:41.260
-I've written
the whole process off.

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:43.429
I think this is a bunch of BS.

00:07:43.429 --> 00:07:45.831
-Man, these guys are so
desperate to suck up to Trump,

00:07:45.831 --> 00:07:47.533
and keep their tee times
at his golf course.

00:07:47.533 --> 00:07:49.701
I mean, look at this photo
of Graham and Paul

00:07:49.701 --> 00:07:50.936
golfing with Trump.

00:07:50.936 --> 00:07:52.671
Rand Paul looks like
the doctor who delivered

00:07:52.671 --> 00:07:54.306
Arnold Schwarzenegger
and Danny DeVito

00:07:54.306 --> 00:07:56.008
in the movie "Twins."

00:07:56.008 --> 00:07:57.643
[ Laughter ]

00:07:57.643 --> 00:08:00.246
Lindsey Graham is making excuses
now because he's getting

00:08:00.246 --> 00:08:01.780
what he wants out of Trump,

00:08:01.780 --> 00:08:03.382
and doesn't care what
laws Trump breaks.

00:08:03.382 --> 00:08:05.217
Today, for example Trump
and Graham got together

00:08:05.217 --> 00:08:07.553
at the White House to brag
about how many judges

00:08:07.553 --> 00:08:08.988
they'd pushed
through the Senate.

00:08:08.988 --> 00:08:11.190
-Lindsey, I'd like to have you
come up and say a few words.

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:12.758
You've been terrific.
Thank you very much.

00:08:12.758 --> 00:08:15.027
[ Applause ]

00:08:15.027 --> 00:08:16.795
-Well, in theory, at 4 o'clock,

00:08:16.795 --> 00:08:18.831
we're going to vote
on two more judges.

00:08:18.831 --> 00:08:21.467
So, I'll move
this thing forward.

00:08:21.467 --> 00:08:23.535
[ Laughter ]

00:08:23.535 --> 00:08:25.004
-"Quick, quick,
I don't have much time.

00:08:25.004 --> 00:08:26.505
I'm about to get impeached.

00:08:26.505 --> 00:08:29.675
I need to get my crimes in."

00:08:29.675 --> 00:08:31.910
Trump and his allies
are desperately trying to out

00:08:31.910 --> 00:08:33.478
the whistle-blower because
they have nothing left.

00:08:33.478 --> 00:08:35.014
Now, they're just ignoring
all the evidence.

00:08:35.014 --> 00:08:36.949
Eventually, Republicans
are going to say, "Sure,

00:08:36.949 --> 00:08:38.184
there was a quid
but there was..."

00:08:38.184 --> 00:08:40.519
-No quo pro.

00:08:40.519 --> 00:08:42.054
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:08:42.054 --> 00:08:44.190
[ Cheers and applause ]

